From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:36:31 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0703): match LAN discovery of address-enrolled peers by
 host ID

AC-20, AC-21, DEF-3 (whole-product review finding 7). A peer enrolled by IP is saved (and
dialled) under its address, but answers LAN discovery with its RustDesk ID, so it never showed
as reachable and, with no ID server, was reported "server unreachable". Saved peers now carry
the pinned host ID (identity option remotesmith-host-id) apart from the connection target:
discovery matches by the host ID, the ID server is asked only about ID-route peers, and an
address-only peer that does not answer on the LAN is "offline (not answering on the LAN)".
A peer saved by IP counts as on the LAN only if its host answered discovery from that IP (any
of the addresses a multihomed host answers from); one
that moved (DHCP) shows "answers on the LAN at <ip>, not at the saved address". A saved peer
whose pin is this machine is not listed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
